:"T"},{"text":" to be stored must be a trivial type. The memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must also be uninitialized, initialized to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"text":", or initialized to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another trivial type that is layout compatible with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeBytes(of:toByteOffset:as:)"},{"text":", the memory is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initialized to the raw bytes of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"text":". If the memory is bound to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U"},{"text":" that is layout compatible with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"text":", then it contains a value of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U"},{"text":". Calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeBytes(of:toByteOffset:as:)"},{"text":" does not change the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound type of the memory.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A trivial type can be copied with just a bit-for-bit copy without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any indirection or reference-counting operations. Generally, native","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift types that do not contain strong or weak references or other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forms of indirection are trivial, as are imported C structs and enums.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to store into memory a copy of a value of a type that isn’t","type":